# One identifier spelling exempted from readability-identifier-naming, inside
# the bookmarks rung's own header tree: `TableName`, the member name the LASTRADA
# Lightweight ORM reads a record's SQL table off. Nothing else is subtracted --
# not a check, not a declaration kind, not a directory's worth of code.
#
# The long form of this argument, and the probe runs behind every claim below,
# are in examples/bank/include/.clang-tidy. This file is the same key applied to
# one more header tree, with this rung's own numbers rather than bank's. The
# short form:
#
#   * The repository-root .clang-tidy sets
#     `readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase: camelBack`, and a Lightweight
#     record has to declare `static constexpr std::string_view TableName`, so
#     every record here is reported as
#     `invalid case style for variable 'TableName'`, offering `tableName`.
#
#   * That rename is a runtime data bug, not a lint fix. `RecordTableNameImpl`
#     in Lightweight/Utils.hpp reads the member by *spelling* --
#     `if constexpr (requires { Record::TableName; })` -- and otherwise falls
#     back to `Reflection::TypeNameOf<Record>`. `tableName` does not fail to
#     compile and does not fail to link: the `requires` clause goes false, the
#     `else` branch runs, and the record is mapped to a table named after the
#     C++ type instead. The first thing that tells anyone is a missing table at
#     run time.
#
#   * An ignore-by-name rather than `-readability-identifier-naming`, because
#     subtracting the check for a directory would stop it measuring every other
#     identifier here.
#
#   * `VariableIgnoredRegexp`, and deliberately not `ClassConstantIgnoredRegexp`
#     or `ConstexprVariableIgnoredRegexp`, which read as more specific and are
#     traps. Naming either of those kinds at all -- even only to set its
#     IgnoredRegexp -- moves the declaration onto a kind with no `Case`
#     configured, so every static constexpr member in reach stops being
#     case-checked whatever it is called. Re-measured for this change with
#     clang-tidy 22.1.8 against a probe header carrying three findings
#     (`TableName`, a second static constexpr member `OtherThing`, and a local
#     `BadLocal`), placed under a rung's include/ and analysed with this
#     repository's real configuration:
#
#       no config here                    TableName, OtherThing, BadLocal
#       VariableIgnoredRegexp             OtherThing, BadLocal
#       ClassConstantIgnoredRegexp        BadLocal only
#       ConstexprVariableIgnoredRegexp    BadLocal only
#
#     `Variable` is the kind the diagnostic itself names ("invalid case style
#     for *variable*"), so setting its IgnoredRegexp changes nothing but the
#     one spelling.
#
#   * `InheritParentConfig: true` is load-bearing, not decoration. Without it
#     clang-tidy *replaces* the root configuration rather than extending it.
#     Measured on the same probe with the key removed and nothing else changed:
#     `Error: no checks enabled.`, exit 1, both from a direct clang-tidy run
#     and through clang-tidy-diff.py. So its absence is a red build with a
#     message naming the problem, not a quietly unlinted directory.
#
# ── Scope, and why it is this directory ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# clang-tidy resolves configuration by walking up from the file it is
# analysing and offers no finer granularity than a directory, so the only
# choice is which directory. One up, at `examples/`, is refused: a config there
# governs every rung's src/, include/ and gui_lib/ together -- a narrow
# suppression in the shape that quietly becomes a wide one. Nothing gates that
# placement, so it is a rule to keep by hand.
#
# `examples/bookmarks/include/` is this rung's own header tree. It holds 23
# .hpp and no .cpp at all, so this file governs declarations and nothing
# else, and none of those headers matches the root `HeaderFilterRegex`
# (`include/morph/.*`) -- so a `TableName` reached from some .cpp is
# discarded as non-user code whatever this file says. The case that reaches
# CI is clang-tidy-diff analysing a *changed header* as a main file, which is
# the only way any of these declarations is judged at all.
#
# Reach on this revision: 5 of the repository's 71 `static constexpr
# std::string_view TableName` declarations are under this directory, one each
# in bookmarks/db/bookmark_entity.hpp, bookmark_tag_entity.hpp,
# imported_op_entity.hpp, outbox_entity.hpp and tag_entity.hpp. Each is
# reported by clang-tidy 22.1.8 without this file and clean with it, measured
# through clang-tidy-diff.py over a real one-line edit. The other
# subdirectories (app/, auth/, core/, dto/, import/, models/, units.hpp) are
# in reach and contain no `TableName`; the ignore has nothing to do there and
# does nothing.
#
# The residue, stated rather than intended: a local variable or ordinary member
# spelled exactly `TableName`, written anywhere under this tree for some reason
# unrelated to the ORM, is not case-checked. Nothing else about it is
# suppressed, no other check is affected, and no other spelling is -- the probe
# table above is the evidence for that.

InheritParentConfig: true

CheckOptions:
  - key:   readability-identifier-naming.VariableIgnoredRegexp
    value: '^TableName$'
